    <string name="help_close">Close</string>
    <string name="help_control">Control blocks (blue) - Start and Stop blocks to begin and end program. Every program must start with a Start block and end with a Stop block. These blocks define the beginning and end of program execution.</string>
    <string name="help_variables">Variables (orange) - Create and manage variables in program. You can create variables of different types (int, double, string, bool), set their values, and modify them. Variables are used to store and manipulate data in program.</string>
    <string name="help_math">Math (light blue) - Perform mathematical operations. Add, subtract, multiply, and divide numbers. You can use both variables and direct values in mathematical operations. The result can be stored in a variable or used in other operations.</string>
    <string name="help_logic">Logic (green) - Use if, else if, and else conditions to control program flow. Create conditions using comparison operators. If the condition is true, the code inside the if block will execute. Use else if for additional conditions and else for the default case.</string>
    <string name="help_io">Input/Output (red) - Print variables to console. Use print blocks to display variable values or text in the console. This is useful for debugging and showing program results to the user.</string>
    <string name="help_debug">Debug mode - Step through program execution one block at a time. This helps you understand how program works and find errors. In debug mode, you can see the values of variables at each step.</string>
    <string name="help_run">Run - Execute program. When you click Run, the program will execute all blocks in sequence from Start to Stop. You can see the results in the console.</string>
    <string name="help_clear">Clear - Remove all blocks from workspace. This is useful when you want to start a new program or remove all blocks to reorganize code.</string>

